<title>CANADA: Canada's dry SE Prairies see up to 4.9 inches rain.</title>
<headline>Canada's dry SE Prairies see up to 4.9 inches rain.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's drought-stricken southeast Prairies received up to 4.9 inches of rain in the 24 hours ended 0700 CDT Wednesday, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>SASKATCHEWAN			ALBERTA</p>
<p>Estevan	45 mm (1.8 inch) Lethbridge 0.5 mm (0.02 inch)</p>
<p>Coronach     21 mm (0.8 inch) Jasper     0.4 mm (0.02 inch)</p>
<p>Benson	 40 mm (1.6 inch) BRITISH COLUMBIA (DAWSON CREEK)</p>
<p>Aneroid	21 mm (0.8 inch) Ft St John 0.6 mm (0.02 inch)</p>
<p>Yellow Grass 16 mm (0.6 inch)</p>
<p>Assiniboia    6 mm (0.2 inch)</p>
<p>Moose Jaw     5 mm (0.2 inch)</p>
<p>Cypress Hills 3 mm (0.1 inch)</p>
<p>MANITOBA</p>
<p>Vita	  124 mm (4.9 inch) Winkler	70 mm (2.8 inch)</p>
<p>Steinbach    67 mm (2.6 inch) Portage	63 mm (2.5 inch)</p>
<p>Brandon	52 mm (2.1 inch) Miami	  52 mm (2.1 inch)</p>
<p>Winnipeg     50 mm (2.0 inch) Pilot Mound  40 mm (1.6 inch)</p>
<p>Virden	 43 mm (1.7 inch) Carman	 40 mm (1.6 inch)</p>
<p>Pierson	33 mm (1.3 inch) Gimli	  34 mm (1.3 inch)</p>
<p>Carberry     26 mm (1.0 inch) Wasagaming   11 mm (0.4 inch)</p>
<p>((Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
